    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0299" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5959</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Military Attaché in Japan (Mcllroy) to the
                        Adjutant General of the Army (Bridges)</hi><anchor n="14" xml:id="d184-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-23">February 23, 1933</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 268. Have reliable information that General Liu<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d184-f2"/> and 10,000 volunteers near Kailu have ceased opposition
                    and pledged allegiance Manchukuo. Japan has begun such military preparations in
                    Bonin and Mandate Islands as she deems it necessary, in the opinion of this
                    office. On February 21st Peipiao was occupied by 31st Infantry 8th Division in
                    face of slight resistance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McIlroy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
